@@ -61,7 +61,7 @@
 <p>Build ten prospect types, not a list of every importer. Use Ukrainian-steel stockholders, Turkish-steel fabricators, aluminium-profile importers, façade-system suppliers, fastening wholesalers, trailer and body builders, greenhouse-structure suppliers, metal furniture makers, fertiliser wholesalers and precast or cement-product importers. Each prospect must have a Dutch entity, a known non-EU supplier, likely annual mass above the threshold and no visible carbon team.</p>
 <p>The route begins with two Dutch customs brokers and one carbon-accounting adviser. Ask each for one anonymised client whose supplier data remain incomplete. The partner should introduce the diagnostic, lead Dutch calls and keep declaration responsibility where already contracted. Start in the Zaandam–Rotterdam logistics corridor, but follow the supplier relationship rather than a postcode.</p>
 <p>The fixed offer is a <strong>€2,000 design hurdle</strong>, 50% in advance. It covers one importer, one installation and one product family. The output is an actual-versus-default cost map, supplier evidence inventory, structured request, two foreign-language supplier sessions and a handover memo. It excludes verification, legal advice, customs correction and final filing.</p>
-<p>The finance or customs lead signs. A stopped shipment is the urgent event; otherwise the decision is whether better data can save more certificate cash than it costs to obtain and verify. The diagnostic must state that saving before proposing a retainer. If default values are cheaper than the full data-and-verification path, recommend the default route and stop.</p>
+<p>The finance or customs lead signs before choosing the data route for the annual declaration. The decision is whether better data can save more certificate cash than it costs to obtain and verify. A customs hold belongs to the broker's authorisation work; it may produce a referral, but this diagnostic cannot resolve it. The diagnostic must state the expected saving before proposing a retainer. If defaults are cheaper than the full data-and-verification path, recommend them and stop.</p>
 <p>The kill fact is only partly settled. Customs Support Group markets customs clearance beside CBAM and EUDR reporting, with more than 1,700 customs experts and 60,000 clients. <!-- CHECK: 02-customs-support --> Deloitte Netherlands markets an integrated service spanning supplier solicitation, validation, authorised declaration and customs brokerage. <!-- CHECK: 02-deloitte-incumbent --> These firms can bundle the work. Neither publishes a comparable small-importer price or says the supplier-data work is free. <!-- CHECK: 02-price-boundary --> Two live broker quotes are still required.</p>
