 <p>Year one is paid discovery. Four diagnostics and two small retainers can fit around a job if supplier calls are scheduled and the broker handles emergencies. It cannot replace developer income. The negative result is deliberate: founder time is not free merely because it is used at night.</p>
 <p>The mature case clears the owner target, but only at recurring prices far above the pitch's original per-shipment idea. A €150 statement fee cannot support senior supplier investigation. The mature CBAM retainer must cover a defined importer portfolio and leave verification outside. The EUDR retainer is lower because Ukraine's low-risk status and state tools reduce work.</p>
-<p>Capacity is the real model. Twenty CBAM clients at one delivery day a month consume 240 days a year. Fifteen EUDR clients at half a day consume another 90. Supplier onboardings add about 45 days. One analyst and one associate provide most routine capacity; the founder sells, qualifies, escalates and reviews. If each mill still consumes founder negotiation every quarter, the table has too few people.</p>
+<p>Capacity is also a design hurdle. One analyst and one associate each get 220 available days after leave: 440 together. A 65% delivery target provides 286 client days and reserves 154 for training, administration, coordination and sales support. None of those figures is observed performance.</p>
+<p>The scoped workload is 282 staff days: twenty CBAM clients at nine days each, fifteen EUDR clients at 4.8 days each, and fifteen supplier onboardings at two days each. The founder adds a 30-day review and escalation hurdle. The carbon specialist adds fifteen technical-review days. Four spare staff-delivery days make this a limit, not comfortable capacity. If quarterly mill negotiation exceeds scope, the table needs another associate or fewer clients.</p>
 <p>Working capital should be almost absent. Bill diagnostics 50% in advance and retainers quarterly in advance. Do not hold certificates or import goods. The <strong>year-one cash-at-risk hurdle is €12,000</strong>, released in stages after payment. Before evidence, spend at most €4,000. That is well below the €50,000 rule and leaves the reader's capital outside this experiment.</p>
 </section>
 
@@ -93,7 +94,7 @@
 <h2>The incumbent gets a turn</h2>
 <p>The customs broker begins with the account, import data, authorisation and border workflow. Customs Support Group explicitly places CBAM and EUDR inside a portfolio of customs clearance, reporting and outsourcing. <!-- CHECK: 02-customs-support --> Deloitte can join supplier data, declaration, certificates and brokerage in one managed service. <!-- CHECK: 02-deloitte-incumbent --> The customer may prefer one accountable counterparty even if its foreign-language follow-up is slower.</p>
 <p>The free substitute is also improving. The CBAM registry carries default values, while the Dutch authority publishes a calculator and guidance. <!-- CHECK: 02-default-route --> A large mill can register its installation once and share a verified record with buyers. A procurement employee can then connect it to customs quantities. Better standards and tooling compress the mechanical work.</p>
-<p>On wood, the Ukrainian state is building the entrant's proposed upstream data service. Its tools expose origin, harvesting documents and geolocation. <!-- CHECK: 02-ukraine-system --> EU reform reduced downstream repetition, and low-risk classification removes full risk assessment in qualifying cases. <!-- CHECK: 02-eudr-revision --> <!-- CHECK: 02-low-risk-effect --> The wood line should be a cheap readiness diagnostic, not a bet on manual polygon retrieval.</p>
+<p>On wood, the Ukrainian agency presents batch-tracking and legality services in response to questions about proving harvest-site geolocation. <!-- CHECK: 02-ukraine-system --> EU reform replaced downstream statement submissions with narrower information duties. <!-- CHECK: 02-eudr-revision --> Qualifying low-risk sourcing removes full risk assessment while preserving information collection. <!-- CHECK: 02-low-risk-effect --> The wood line should be a cheap readiness diagnostic, not a bet on manual polygon retrieval.</p>
 <p>The partner-capture response is structural. A broker gives the entrant two difficult suppliers, observes the protocol, then hires a Russian-speaking coordinator or sends the rest to Deloitte's tooling. The entrant never owned authorisation or the importer. Its defence is a cross-broker installation library and faster CEE resolution. Both depend on permissions the partner may refuse.</p>
 </section>
 
