 <p>Regulatory literacy supplies the boundary. It separates threshold, authorisation, actual values, default values, verification and certificate cash. The engineering habit turns an email chase into a data lineage: quantity to customs entry, good to code, product to installation, installation to process, process to source record. Internal automation can reduce errors, but the customer buys a signed handover pack, not access to a tool.</p>
 <p>The Dutch-language gate is conditional, not passed. No Dutch trade exam appears in the CBAM roles reviewed here; the legal roles are importer, authorised declarant, indirect representative and accredited verifier. <!-- CHECK: 02-credential-boundary --> The operator's technical emissions report must be submitted in English under the implementing regulation. <!-- CHECK: 02-english-report --> That helps with the mill. It does not make A2 sufficient for Dutch cold sales, customs disputes or a finance director's risk questions.</p>
 <p>The answer is a Dutch customs partner. The partner owns the local relationship, customs representation and Dutch explanation. The entrant contracts as its named CEE supplier-data specialist. Customs confirms that a service party may deliver the CBAM filing on the importer's behalf through chain authorisation, while the importer remains liable. <!-- CHECK: 02-service-provider-role --> If the partner insists on owning the method, supplier relationship and all margin, the channel fails.</p>
-<p>Ingdilligenz GmbH in Würzburg is the precedent. Its own site markets import-data analysis, supplier communication, emissions support, XML preparation and report submission as a CBAM representative. <!-- CHECK: 02-precedent-offer --> An independent register trace records HRB 15952, incorporation on 17 November 2021 and €25,000 share capital. <!-- CHECK: 02-precedent-trace --> This proves that a small firm can persist on the shape. It does not establish Dutch prices, independence from software or payment for the language layer.</p>
+<p>Ingdilligenz GmbH in Würzburg is the precedent. Its own site markets import-data analysis, supplier communication, emissions support, XML preparation and report submission as a CBAM representative. <!-- CHECK: 02-precedent-offer --> An independent trace records HRB 15952, articles dated 17 November 2021, a register notice published 20 November and €25,000 share capital. <!-- CHECK: 02-precedent-trace --> Together, the records establish a real small-firm precedent for the offer's shape. They do not establish commercial persistence, customers, Dutch prices or payment for the language layer.</p>
 <p>The constraint that breaks the fit is the buyer side. If the reader cannot find a Dutch broker willing to lead meetings and retain the importer contract, A2 makes direct acquisition brittle. If the reader wants physical site work, this also fails personally. It is desk work attached to metal, and the least physical candidate in the book.</p>
 </section>
 
@@ -61,7 +61,7 @@
 <p>Build ten prospect types, not a list of every importer. Use Ukrainian-steel stockholders, Turkish-steel fabricators, aluminium-profile importers, façade-system suppliers, fastening wholesalers, trailer and body builders, greenhouse-structure suppliers, metal furniture makers, fertiliser wholesalers and precast or cement-product importers. Each prospect must have a Dutch entity, a known non-EU supplier, likely annual mass above the threshold and no visible carbon team.</p>
 <p>The route begins with two Dutch customs brokers and one carbon-accounting adviser. Ask each for one anonymised client whose supplier data remain incomplete. The partner should introduce the diagnostic, lead Dutch calls and keep declaration responsibility where already contracted. Start in the Zaandam–Rotterdam logistics corridor, but follow the supplier relationship rather than a postcode.</p>
 <p>The fixed offer is a <strong>€2,000 design hurdle</strong>, 50% in advance. It covers one importer, one installation and one product family. The output is an actual-versus-default cost map, supplier evidence inventory, structured request, two foreign-language supplier sessions and a handover memo. It excludes verification, legal advice, customs correction and final filing.</p>
-<p>The finance or customs lead signs. A stopped shipment is the urgent event; otherwise the decision is whether better data can save more certificate cash than it costs to obtain and verify. The diagnostic must state that saving before proposing a retainer. If default values are cheaper than the full data-and-verification path, recommend the default route and stop.</p>
+<p>The finance or customs lead signs before choosing the data route for the annual declaration. The decision is whether better data can save more certificate cash than it costs to obtain and verify. A customs hold belongs to the broker's authorisation work; it may produce a referral, but this diagnostic cannot resolve it. The diagnostic must state the expected saving before proposing a retainer. If defaults are cheaper than the full data-and-verification path, recommend them and stop.</p>
 <p>The kill fact is only partly settled. Customs Support Group markets customs clearance beside CBAM and EUDR reporting, with more than 1,700 customs experts and 60,000 clients. <!-- CHECK: 02-customs-support --> Deloitte Netherlands markets an integrated service spanning supplier solicitation, validation, authorised declaration and customs brokerage. <!-- CHECK: 02-deloitte-incumbent --> These firms can bundle the work. Neither publishes a comparable small-importer price or says the supplier-data work is free. <!-- CHECK: 02-price-boundary --> Two live broker quotes are still required.</p>
