6. **Mature capacity — fixed.** The economics section now bridges two staff at a 220-day design hurdle each, 65% delivery utilisation, 286 delivery days, 154 non-delivery days and a 282-day scoped workload. It separately budgets 30 founder review days and fifteen specialist days, exposes four staff days of slack, and states when another associate or fewer clients are required. Every figure is labelled as a design hurdle.

7. **Default-route receipt — fixed.** `resources/sources/02/excerpts/02-default-route.txt` now includes the NEa passages for the cost calculator and registry inclusion. The TSV claim and locator were expanded to cover both chapter uses.

8. **Marker placement — fixed.** The Ukraine low-risk marker now immediately follows its sentence; the low-risk-effect and EUDR markers follow their own claims. Repeated markers were also placed directly after the actual-verification and installation-registry claims where those facts recur.

